    <item>
      <title>AI Briefing: Anthropic Didn't Build a New Browser. They Did Something Sma</title>
      <description>AI Summary:
Today, we’re diving into the powerful capabilities of the Claude extension for Chrome, a tool that integrates a large language model right into your browser. By harnessing Claude, you can delegate repetitive tasks—saving you hours each week from tedious online chores, like negotiating with customer service or gathering analytics. Imagine opening a live chat with your internet provider and letting Claude handle the dialogue, pushing for that refund without you lifting a finger.

The extension also allows you to record workflows, automating tasks like checking emails or pulling data from various websites. You can set up recurring shortcuts for tasks you do regularly, transforming your productivity. Plus, Claude is built to seamlessly navigate popular platforms like Gmail and Google Drive, making inbox triage and document organization a breeze. 

With Claude, you gain a valuable ally to streamline your online tasks, all from the convenience of your browser, making it an essential tool for anyone looking to work smarter, not harder.</description>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Mar 2026 16:58:27 GMT</pubDate>
      <enclosure url="https://obrien-private-podcast.onrender.com/audio/Anthropic_Didn't_Build_a_New_Browser._They_Did_Something_Sma.m4a" type="audio/mp4" length="10000000"/>
